 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "On one island in the Pacific,",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 1.7
  },
  {
   "text": "the mailman had to swim.",
   "s": 1.916,
   "e": 3.468
  },
  {
   "text": "Niuafo'ou is a volcano with no harbor,",
   "s": 4.132,
   "e": 6.906
  },
  {
   "text": "and the surf is too rough for ships to land.",
   "s": 7.105,
   "e": 9.356
  },
  {
   "text": "So when a steamship appeared,",
   "s": 9.847,
   "e": 11.283
  },
  {
   "text": "the strongest swimmers paddled out,",
   "s": 11.569,
   "e": 13.323
  },
  {
   "text": "holding the island's letters up on long poles.",
   "s": 13.599,
   "e": 16.056
  },
  {
   "text": "The crew lifted the letters aboard in buckets.",
   "s": 16.607,
   "e": 18.945
  },
  {
   "text": "Then they sealed the island's new mail inside a biscuit tin,",
   "s": 19.28,
   "e": 22.458
  },
  {
   "text": "and threw it into the sea.",
   "s": 22.668,
   "e": 23.894
  },
  {
   "text": "The swimmers fought the waves,",
   "s": 24.491,
   "e": 25.988
  },
  {
   "text": "grabbed the floating tin,",
   "s": 26.129,
   "e": 27.314
  },
  {
   "text": "and pushed it all the way back to shore.",
   "s": 27.487,
   "e": 29.453
  },
  {
   "text": "No dock.",
   "s": 29.956,
   "e": 30.571
  },
  {
   "text": "No boat.",
   "s": 30.765,
   "e": 31.364
  },
  {
   "text": "Just a tin can and a very good swimmer.",
   "s": 31.725,
   "e": 34.11
  },
  {
   "text": "Letters sometimes took months.",
   "s": 34.725,
   "e": 36.619
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the world noticed.",
   "s": 37.201,
   "e": 38.618
  },
  {
   "text": "Collectors everywhere wanted a letter stamped on that tiny island.",
   "s": 38.971,
   "e": 42.448
  },
  {
   "text": "Soon it had a new name:",
   "s": 42.886,
   "e": 44.183
  },
  {
   "text": "Tin Can Island.",
   "s": 44.621,
   "e": 45.858
  },
  {
   "text": "An island with no harbor became famous for its post office.",
   "s": 46.397,
   "e": 50.069
  }
 ]
}